A||||12||FNXRISING||Aura Bass Shakers-- Anybody use them?||||1||
Z||000000||FNXRISING||01-09-2001||02:25 AM||||Hey everybody!  Thanks for all of the help with my TCC problem.  Most helpful!<P>I will be changing my stock stereo and speakers out very soon.  Have any of you either heard about or used Aura Bass Shakers?  I read about them in Popular Mechanics some years ago, and they sounded interesting.  Apparently they are about the size of a hockey puck and mount below your seats on the sub-frame.  They resonate instead of having to push air like woofers do, and supposedly offer amazing sub bass will very little power necessary.  I almost got some for my Delorean, but it never worked out.  I'm wondering, if they are so simple, affordable, effective, etc., why don't I hear more about them?...Are they too good to be true?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dj_yellow88-sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||01-09-2001||09:05 AM||||I have two sets of them in my home surround sound systems.  They are awesome for movie effects.  They make you jump right out of your seat.  I have them bolted to the bottom of the sofas. They are bigger than hocky pucks about a 6inch diameter and about two inches high.  They don't need much of an amplifier about 25 watts. I have been wanting to put some in my car but haven't tried it yet. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||01-09-2001||09:19 AM||||a friend of mine has them in his 914-6. (not a factory 6) it's AWSOME! they make your eyeballs shake!! and not annoying to other drivers! get em!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||01-09-2001||09:23 AM||||I have a set in my car.  The do add to the effect but are no replacement for a subwoofer.  I think the reason they are not popular is first, they gotta be mounted to work.  In a stereo shop, they usually do not go out of the way to set up a display for them.  Secondly, they are not as sexy as some bigass woofers. If the kids don't buy it, don't matter how good they work.  But they do work, and since they aren't very popular,theycan be gotten cheaply.<p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||CraZyRabBit||01-09-2001||11:20 AM||||Question I have about them is...will they fit under the Fiero seats without contact when you sit?||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||01-09-2001||02:33 PM||||Well, you must trim carpet away under the seat. They do need to be mounted directly to metal surface. There is enough room to fit, and I don't feel any lump under the foam (and at 280, I compress that foam pretty well!) The issue I ran into is that it does interfere with seat travel some, but not enough to make it unworkable. Just takes some finesse.||||reg||1
Z||000006||286SE'S||01-09-2001||04:00 PM||||Hope you can still find them. It seems they were dumped on to the surplus market and were selling for $9.95. I tried to order them and they were sold out. This was in October 2000 at partsexpress.com (just checked again and they were not found in a search) MCM electronics may still have some but their website does not work on word searches just part numbers, so you need a catalog. I also have the "mounted to the sofa" set; they are great and not annoying outside the room.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Xtreme Fiero's||01-09-2001||06:03 PM||||the AURA shakers will resonate (sp) the car at IT'S peak level witch is much lower on a all steel car than a Fiero when my car was metered it peaked @ 60hz while my steel truck was down around 33hz this means that the bass will be loudest around 75hz in a fiero the human ean can't hear below 60hz so any bass above 60hz would be heard from the "Speaker" not the car in depending on the resonant (SP) Freq. of your can it may sound like crap or it may sound awsome. Solid Tight cars will have a higher freq. while looseer cars w/ large flat areas of sheet metal wil hit lower.<P>P.S. when they are in the right car they sound awsome. take your car to a local Car audio shop (not Best Buy) to get your cars Resonant (someone please spell it right) SPL metered.||||reg||1
Z||000008||stsmithgt||01-09-2001||06:50 PM||||I just saw a similar speaker on TechTV.  Being a new design, it probably isn't cheap.  I can't remeber the name of it because they kept calling it the butt pounder.  They had it mounted under a bar stood cushion.  Anyway, these things mounted with a single bolt in the middle on one side.  It looked like it would fit easily somewhere in the car.  Car audio might not be the only place to look for these since they were talking about there home system.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Philphine||01-09-2001||07:03 PM||||i've got a pair in my chevy but i've only had them hooked up temporarily. seemed pretty helpful since there's not much room for a big sub system. if i ever finish i can give a better opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000010||varnster||01-09-2001||10:02 PM||||since were on the subject of small, diameter<BR>bass what about the infinity bass link, I saw<BR>it in crutchfield, its a powered 10 inch,<BR>has any one heard this joker.||||reg||1
Z||000011||FIEROGOD||01-10-2001||08:35 PM|||| Bass shakers are cool. A buddy had them in his 88 sport poop. They don't produce any sound but they make it feel like you have a pair of 10s in there. Alpine makes them also. I have a 6 inch bass tube in my SE. I like it better than the 10 in my sister's 86 sport poop.||||reg||1
Z||000012||mope||01-11-2001||06:46 PM||||i just did a search on yahoo and found out these things cost more than 100 bucks each.<P>m0pe||||reg||1
